        "original_id": "e297ccda-2838-598d-add3-3829f80f9aa2",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Elizabeth Wordsworth, Christopher Wordsworth, John Wordsworth\n- Organizations: St Hugh's College, Oxford, Anglican Church\n- Roles: Bishop of Lincoln, Bishop of Salisbury, liturgical scholar, founder\n\nFacts:\n- Christopher Wordsworth was born on 30 October 1807 and died on 20 March 1885.\n- Christopher Wordsworth was an English bishop in the Anglican Church and a man of letters.\n- Elizabeth Wordsworth was the daughter of Christopher Wordsworth, who was Bishop of Lincoln.\n- Elizabeth Wordsworth was the sister of John Wordsworth, who was Bishop of Salisbury, and of Christopher Wordsworth, who was a liturgical scholar.\n- St Hugh's College, Oxford, was founded in 1886 by Elizabeth Wordsworth as a women's college.\n- St Hugh's College, Oxford, accepted its first male students in 1986, its centenary year.",
